---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageContainer from '../../components/ui/PageContainer.astro';
import Section from '../../components/ui/Section.astro';
import { contact } from '../../data/navigation';

/*
 * Every statement here describes behaviour that exists in this codebase and
 * was verified in the browser. Nothing is asserted about WMC's internal
 * handling of enquiries — retention, storage and erasure are WMC's to state,
 * so this page directs those questions to WMC rather than inventing answers.
 */
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | West Midlands Coaches"
  description="How West Midlands Coaches handles the information you provide through the quotation and contact forms on this website."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <Section as="div" surface="warm-white">
    <PageContainer>
      <article class="legal">
        <header class="legal__head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
          <h1 class="text-h2 legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="text-body-large legal__lead">
            This policy explains what happens to the information you enter on this website. It
            covers the website only.
          </p>
          <p class="text-small legal__meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
        </header>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            {contact.registeredName} (trading as {contact.companyName}), a company registered in
            England and Wales, company number {contact.companyNumber}, registered at{' '}
            {contact.address}. WMC is the data controller for information submitted through this
            website.
          </p>
          <p>
            To ask anything about this policy, or to make a request about your information, contact
            WMC on <a class="legal__link" href={contact.phoneHref}>{contact.phoneDisplay}</a> or
            through the details on the{' '}
            <a class="legal__link" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">What we collect, and when</h2>
          <p>
            This website collects information only when you choose to submit one of its two forms.
            There is no account system, and nothing is collected from you simply by browsing.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-h6">Quotation request form</h3>
          <p>
            The <a class="legal__link" href="/request-a-quote/">quotation form</a> collects the
            journey details you enter: pickup and destination, any additional stops, dates and
            times, return journey details, passenger numbers, luggage requirements, service level
            and vehicle preference, journey purpose, how you heard about WMC, any additional notes
            you write, and your contact details — name, organisation, email address, telephone
            number and preferred contact method.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-h6">Contact form</h3>
          <p>
            The <a class="legal__link" href="/contact/">contact form</a> collects your name, email
            address, telephone number if you provide one, the enquiry type you select, and your
            message.
          </p>

          <p>
            We ask for this information so WMC can understand the journey, prepare a quotation and
            reply to you. The lawful basis is your request: processing is necessary to take steps
            at your request before entering into a contract, and in WMC's legitimate interest in
            responding to enquiries.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">How your form submission reaches WMC</h2>
          <p>
            This is a static website with no database and no server of its own. When you submit
            either form, your browser sends the form contents directly to{' '}
            <a
              class="legal__link"
              href="https://web3forms.com/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Web3Forms
            </a>, a third-party form-delivery service, which emails the submission to WMC. Web3Forms
            therefore processes your submission in transit, and their own privacy terms apply to
            that step.
          </p>
          <p>
            After that, your enquiry sits in WMC's email inbox like any other email. This website
            keeps no copy of it. How long WMC keeps enquiry emails, and how to ask for yours to be
            deleted, is a question for WMC directly using the contact details above.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you choose WhatsApp as your preferred contact method, after your submission has been
            confirmed the site opens WhatsApp with a short summary of the journey ready to send —
            route, dates, times, passenger numbers, service level and vehicle preference. You choose
            whether to send it. That summary deliberately excludes your email address, your notes,
            your organisation and how you heard about WMC. Sending it puts the message into
            WhatsApp, and WhatsApp's own terms apply to it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">Address suggestions from Google</h2>
          <p>
            The pickup, destination and stop fields on the quotation form offer address suggestions.
            To do that, the text you type into those fields is sent to Google's Places service as
            you type, and Google returns matching places. Google receives that text, and your IP
            address, as part of the request; Google's own privacy policy applies to it.
          </p>
          <p>
            This only happens on the quotation page, only in the address fields, and only once you
            have typed at least three characters. If Google is unavailable or blocked, the fields
            keep working as ordinary text boxes and you can type an address by hand.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">Saving your progress</h2>
          <p>
            While you are filling in the quotation form, your answers are kept in your own browser's
            session storage so that moving between the three steps, or reloading the page by
            accident, does not lose your work. This stays on your device, is never sent anywhere by
            the website itself, and is deleted as soon as your request is submitted successfully or
            when you close the tab.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">What we do not do</h2>
          <ul class="legal__list">
            <li>No analytics or visitor tracking of any kind.</li>
            <li>No advertising, remarketing or profiling.</li>
            <li>No marketing emails; WMC replies to your enquiry, and nothing more.</li>
            <li>Your details are not sold, rented or shared for marketing.</li>
            <li>
              No cookies are set by this website — see the{' '}
              <a class="legal__link" href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Under UK data protection law you have the right to ask what information WMC holds about
            you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict how it is used, and to
            receive a copy of it. Contact WMC using the details above to make a request.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are not satisfied with the response, you can complain to the Information
            Commissioner's Office at{' '}
            <a
              class="legal__link"
              href="https://ico.org.uk/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              ico.org.uk
            </a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal__section">
          <h2 class="text-h4">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If this website's handling of your information changes, this page will be updated and
            the date at the top will change with it.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </PageContainer>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-inline-size: 68ch;
  }

  .legal__head {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal__title {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .legal__lead {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .legal__meta {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-slate-taupe);
  }

  .legal__section {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal__section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--color-obsidian);
  }

  .legal__section h3 {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-1);
    color: var(--color-obsidian);
  }

  .legal__section p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .legal__section p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .legal__list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-3);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .legal__link {
    color: var(--color-obsidian);
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-champagne-gold);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .legal__link:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-obsidian);
  }
</style>
